"401892617000006010","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Emil Heineman Game Misconduct","type":{"id":"93","text":"Game Misconduct","abbreviation":"Game misconduct"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:22"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"12"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4697447","displayName":"Emil Heineman","shortName":"E. Heineman"}}]},{"id":"401892617000000790","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Leon Draisaitl faceoff won against Jean-Gabriel Pageau","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:22"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"6"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3114727","displayName":"Leon Draisaitl","shortName":"L. Draisaitl"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"2593131","displayName":"Jean-Gabriel Pageau","shortName":"J. Pageau"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"7226","fullName":"UBS Arena","address":{"city":"Elmont","state":"NY","zipCode":"11003","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/7226.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":16587,"officials":[{"fullName":"Scott Cherrey","displayName":"Scott Cherrey","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kyle Rehman","displayName":"Kyle Rehman","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Justin Kea","displayName":"Justin Kea","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Onni Hautamaki","displayName":"Onni Hautamaki","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Connor McDavid extends his assist streak to 14 games as the Oilers beat the Islanders 4-0","description":"— Connor McDavid extended his NHL-record season-opening assist streak to 14 games by setting up Ryan Nugent-Hopkins' second goal, and the Edmonton Oilers opened their road trip by beating the New York Islanders 4-0 on Saturday.","story":"NEW YORK -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3895074/connor-mcdavid\">Connor McDavid</a> extended his NHL-record season-opening assist streak to 14 games by setting up <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562624/ryan-nugent-hopkins\">Ryan Nugent-Hopkins</a>' second goal, and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/edm/edmonton-oilers\">Edmonton Oilers</a> opened their road trip by beating the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyi/new-york-islanders\">New York Islanders</a> 4-0 on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              Nugent-Hopkins scored on a power play in the third period to give McDavid his league-best 29th assist. No other NHL player has that many goals and assists combined, and McDavid has a big lead in points with 37 — and is on pace for more than 200.\n\n\r\n              Longtime running mate <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114727/leon-draisaitl\">Leon Draisaitl</a> recorded a pair of assists, including a perfect skate-to-stick exchange that led to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565231/vasily-podkolzin\">Vasily Podkolzin</a> putting the puck into a wide open net. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3151981/ilya-sorokin\">Ilya Sorokin</a> similarly had little chance on Nugent-Hopkins' shot from point-blank range off a feed from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114775/kasperi-kapanen\">Kasperi Kapanen</a> 68 seconds earlier.\n\n\r\n              Edmonton's <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042020/tristan-jarry\">Tristan Jarry</a> stopped all 18 shots he faced for a second consecutive shutout, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042062/jason-dickinson\">Jason Dickinson</a> scored into an empty net to seal the victory. The Oilers have won 10 of their first 14 games this season, their first with <a href=\"https://apnews.com/cdb5ab2a34888dea0bdca029e8a2e920\">Mike Babcock as coach</a>.\n\n\r\n              Despite 20 saves from Sorokin, the Islanders' winning streak ended at two games, with top defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291933/matthew-schaefer\">Matthew Schaefer</a> getting whistled for two of the team's five minor penalties. Forward <a href=\"https://apnews.com/df042d614ab0bb2a6b00aa59fff889b9\"><a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697447/emil-heineman\">Emil Heineman</a> was ejected</a> less than 2 1/2 minutes in for a knee-on-knee hit that injured <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080179/isaac-howard\">Isaac Howard</a>, who put no weight on his left leg as he was helped off the ice and did not return.\n\n\r\n              New York was without defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042019/ryan-pulock\">Ryan Pulock</a>, who was seeing a doctor after leaving Thursday night at Minnesota with what the team called an upper-body injury.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Oilers: Make their second stop on a three-game visit to the area by playing at the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a> on Sunday.\n\n\r\n              Islanders: After some time off, host the defending Stanley Cup-champion <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/car/carolina-hurricanes\">Carolina Hurricanes</a> on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-31T20:42:46Z"}}